@startuml release-pipelines
!include _theme.iuml
hide footbox

actor Maintainer
participant "Octoform repository" as AppRepo
participant "Application CI" as AppCI
participant "npm registry" as NPM
participant "GitHub Releases" as Releases
participant "Documentation repository" as DocsRepo
participant "Documentation CI" as DocsCI
participant "GitHub Pages" as Pages

Maintainer -> AppRepo : merge reviewed PR to vMAJOR.x
AppRepo -> AppCI : protected branch push
AppCI -> AppCI : read package version and check tag
AppCI -> AppRepo : create annotated vX.Y.Z tag
AppCI -> AppCI : dispatch release workflow on tag
AppCI -> AppCI : validate tag, changelog, build, tests and package
AppCI -> NPM : OIDC trusted publish with provenance
NPM --> AppCI : immutable package version
AppCI -> Releases : create verified-tag release

Maintainer -> DocsRepo : merge matching documentation PR
DocsRepo -> DocsCI : documentation verification
DocsCI -> DocsCI : lint, build, examples, UML, links, privacy, WCAG
Maintainer -> DocsCI : dispatch docs MAJOR.MINOR\nfor exact app MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
DocsCI -> DocsCI : validate release identity and rebuild
DocsCI -> DocsRepo : mike deploy immutable version\nand latest/stable aliases
DocsCI -> Pages : deploy complete gh-pages history
Pages --> Maintainer : versioned public documentation

note over NPM, Pages
  Application publishing follows the version-branch merge automatically.
  Documentation publishing is an explicit, version-paired dispatch.
end note
@enduml
